- How do embedding size and padding affect numerical stability and softmax behavior?

## Why This Is Asked

To assess the ability to design policy-aware, scalable agent orchestration that handles multi-tenant data isolation and observability.

## Key Concepts

- LangChain agent orchestration with AutoGen planning
- Private APIs and data catalog integration
- Policy enforcement and tenant isolation
- End-to-end traceability, auditing, and failure handling
- Resilience patterns: retries, backoff, circuit breakers

## Code Example

```javascript
async function plan(request) {
  const { userId, tenantId, dataScope } = request;

  const policyResult = await policyEngine.check({ tenantId, dataScope });
  if (!policyResult.allowed) {
    throw new Error('Access denied: policy violation');
  }

  const catalogResult = await dataCatalog.query({ tenantId, dataScope });
  const apiResult = await privateApi.fetch({ tenantId, dataScope });

  await auditLogger.log({
    tenantId,
    userId,
    steps: [policyResult, catalogResult, apiResult],
    traceId: uuid()
  });

  return { data: apiResult, traceId: traceId };
}
```

This flow ensures tenant-scoped policies are enforced at entry, each component call is traced, and failures are handled with compensating transactions or graceful degradation.

